### Sample requests for the Chatex API.
### Run the API with `dotnet run --project Chatex.Api --launch-profile http`,
### then send "Register" (or "Login"); later requests reuse its access token.

@host = http://localhost:5214

### Register
# @name register
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userName": "alice",
  "email": "alice@example.test",
  "password": "Passw0rd!",
  "displayName": "Alice"
}

### Login (user name or email)
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "login": "alice",
  "password": "Passw0rd!"
}

### Refresh (uses the chatex_refresh cookie set by register/login)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/refresh

### My profile
GET {{host}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{register.response.body.accessToken}}

### Search users
GET {{host}}/api/users?query=al
Authorization: Bearer {{register.response.body.accessToken}}

### Create a group
# @name group
POST {{host}}/api/chats
Authorization: Bearer {{register.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "group",
  "title": "Team",
  "description": "Our first group"
}

### My chats
GET {{host}}/api/chats
Authorization: Bearer {{register.response.body.accessToken}}

### Send a message
POST {{host}}/api/chats/{{group.response.body.id}}/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{register.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "Hello, team!"
}

### History (newest first; pass nextCursor as ?before= for older pages)
GET {{host}}/api/chats/{{group.response.body.id}}/messages?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{register.response.body.accessToken}}

### Upload an attachment (then send its id in attachmentIds)
POST {{host}}/api/attachments
Authorization: Bearer {{register.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="notes.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

Some notes.
--boundary--

### Logout (ends the cookie's session)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/logout
